# Graphify indexing exclusions for ClashBot.
#
# Graphify already honours .gitignore, and .gitignore already excludes data/ -- so the secrets
# under {deck}/data/ are skipped twice over. This file is the belt to that pair of braces: it is
# what `--no-gitignore` PRIORITISES, so it is the only exclusion that still holds if someone runs
# with .gitignore disabled.
#
# The standing rule this protects: never commit {deck}/data/. That directory holds the Discord
# webhook (icebow/data/discord_webhook.txt), session recordings, labelled detector datasets and
# policy checkpoints.

# --- secrets and per-deck working data (NEVER index, NEVER commit) ---
data/
**/data/
*webhook*
*.token
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*

# --- large regenerable artifacts: nothing to learn from, and they bloat the graph ---
runs/
annotation_export*/
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mkv
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.zip

# --- graphify's own output, so a rebuild never re-indexes the previous graph ---
graphify-out/
raw/

# --- caches ---
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- card-art template images (added 2026-08-29) ---
# MEASURED: an incremental detect found 4,568 changed images -- 2,335 in hogeq/templates and
# 2,226 in icebow/templates. These are card-recognition template crops: there is nothing semantic
# in them, and graphify gives EVERY image its own vision subagent, so indexing them would have
# dispatched ~4,500 agents for zero graph value. They are regenerable from the sprite bank.
templates/
**/templates/

# --- /watchvideo run folders: contact sheets + source video. The transcript is the artifact
# --- worth reading, and it is already summarised in video-analytics/*/ markdown.
video-analytics/
